ving the first pk you know  there's no other feeling like it because  the other team sees that all of a sudden  it puts doubt in their heads then the  second pk after the second save you know  after that my emotions just went you  know haywire and that's when it all came  out and uh the boys did the rest they  had to score the goals so pressure was  on them for me it was more so just  trying to help them yeah you're like my  job's done they say once you once you  save one you should win the game yeah  you save two yeah so i i saved one then  their goalkeeper saved one which is very  rare the first you know first couple  saves there but saving two i think we  had a pretty good chance of winning it  all yeah for sure  so now you guys are the bringing back  the first championship to new york in a  decade really since the giants won in  2011. what does that mean to you guys  yeah it means the world to us i think  you know to be a part of history in the  city um you know for this club you know  like you said ten years in the making  for for the city it's a sports city um  you know all the all the fans that have  such high expectations um you know  there's been a drought for a while um  you know for our club i've been here for  five years and to bring you know the  first mls cup back to this city the  first in 10 years means everything  because i know how much it means to the  city and the fans and to do it in the  fashion we did it  you know it's something something that's  you know only dreamt about and now it's  reality  so how many championships do you think  you have to want to be the new captain  of new york i mean you play in yankee  stadium ah that's a good question yeah  we'll start with one we'll start with  one and go from there but you know  that's the expectation we're gonna enjoy  this enjoy the moment surrounding you  know the first but we also know that  it's the standard now you know that's  going to be the expectation that's how  new york fans are they get one they want  more uh we obviously want more as well  so we're committed to doing that but i  think right now i think you have to  enjoy these moments because you never  know how long it's going to take to  happen again for sure absolutely so  soccer is the world's favorite sport  america's had some struggle with keeping  it  as popular as other sports but the mls  has really grown a lot in the last  couple of years  you said you've been with the team for  five years you've been in the league  longer than that how have you seen the  change from the way fans come to the  games now engagement from what it was  when you first joined to now in 2021  yeah so you know i came in the league  back in  2010 was my first year so you know 12  years in the making for me it's been uh  tremendous to see the growth of soccer  in this league  when i came into the league  you know the the standard uh how things  were done the quality of players the  quality of play all those things have  increased tenfold and and to see  where we are now  as a country soccer wise as a city  soccer wise is incredible so i think  you're going to see that continue to  increase you know we have the world cup  coming  you know next year and then hosting a  world cup in 2026 so i think in the next  you know five six years you're going to  see a real boom if you haven't before  and  it's just incredible that you know our  country is going to be kind of you know  a cornerstone of what's going to be  looked at as you know i think a soccer  mecca i think we're on the way oh you  think so i think right there with  england and germany and all brazil  everyone i don't think we're far off i  don't think we're off we uh you know now  we're starting to compete teams are  starting to compete on another level we  have a concacaf champions league  that we play in it's a league of  champions with our current region and  mls teams are done a fantastic job and i  think you'll start to see  our teams be respected on a 